  "content": {
    "title": "What teams are left in March Madness? Men's NCAA Tournament bracket updates",
    "text": "March 27, 2026Updated March 28, 2026, 11:46 p.m. ETWhat began as a 68-team Men's NCAA Tournament is now an eight-team March Madness field.The Final Four is beginning to come into focus, with the South and West brackets complete and the East and Midwest brackets set to conclude Sunday, March 29.No. 3 Illinois was able to continue to ride Keaton Wagler and Andrej Stojakovic over No. 9 Iowa to stop the surging Hawkeyes. Wagler and Stojakovic put up 25 and 17 points, respectively, to put Illinois in its first Final Four 2005. Another team partying like it's the aughts was Arizona, which got 20 points from Koa Peat and had another three players in double figures to defeat Purdue and make its first semifinal since 2001.On Sunday, March 29, another two No. 1 seeds will be in their respective bracket finals: Duke after surviving St. John's and Michigan after handily dispatching Alabama. Florida was eliminated by Iowa in the second round, before the Hawkeyes were able to beat Nebraska in the Sweet 16.No. 2 UConn held off a furious Michigan State comeback after an abysmal start for the Spartans, ultimately outlasting them 67-63. The Huskies and Blue Devils will face off Sunday, March 29.Michigan will face No. 6 Tennessee, which was able to defeat Iowa State to make its third straight Elite Eight. The Vols are still seeking their first ever Final Four appearance.As March Madness continues to unfold, USA TODAY Sports will bring minute-to-minute coverage of the entire tournament, including on-site reporting from a handful of its reporters.What teams are still left in March Madness?Here's a look at the teams still dancing in the Men's NCAA Tournament, including those that play in the Sweet 16 on Friday:East RegionNo. 1 Duke (advanced to Elite Eight after beating No. 5 St. John's in Sweet 16)No. 2 UConn (advanced to Elite Eight after beating No. 3 Michigan State in Sweet 16)South RegionNo. 3 Illinois (Won South Region over No. 9 Iowa to advance to Final Four)Midwest RegionNo. 1 Michigan (advanced to Elite Eight after beating No. 4 Alabama in Sweet 16)No. 6 Tennessee (advanced to Elite Eight after beating No. 2 Iowa State in Sweet 16)West RegionNo. 1 Arizona (Won West Region over No. 2 Purdue to advance to Final Four)March Madness schedule today: Friday's Sweet 16 games in Men's NCAA TournamentFriday, March 27All times EasternNo. 1 Duke 80, No. 5 St. John's 75No. 1 Michigan 90, No. 4 Alabama 77No. 2 UConn 67, No. 3 Michigan State 63No. 6 Tennessee 76, No. 2 Iowa State 62Stream select March Madness games with Fubo (free trial) Stream select March Madness games with Sling TVElite Eight schedule for Men's NCAA TournamentClick here to view how the Elite Eight schedule is shaping up and when the regional final games are set to be played.Saturday, March 28No. 3 Illinois 71, No. 9 Iowa 59No. 1 Arizona 79, No. 2 Purdue 64Sunday, March 29No. 1 Michigan vs No. 6 Tennessee | (CBS) | 2:15 p.m. ET | (Fubo, free trial)No. 1 Duke vs No. 2 UConn | (CBS) | 5:05 p.m. ET | (Fubo, free trial)",
